WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.771
- [Ray] I think I'm done.

00:00:01.771 --> 00:00:04.640
- [Maggie] Ahhhh, I need
maybe like five more hours.

00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:07.810
(jazzy music)

00:00:07.810 --> 00:00:10.310
- [Ray] I have probably
twenty different types

00:00:10.310 --> 00:00:11.530
of piping tips.

00:00:11.530 --> 00:00:15.130
I use anything from Macarons,
Kit Kats, and I've gotten

00:00:15.130 --> 00:00:17.210
really good at making a really nice drip

00:00:17.210 --> 00:00:18.910
on the side of most of my cakes.

00:00:18.910 --> 00:00:20.430
- [Maggie] I do a little
bit of baking for fun

00:00:20.430 --> 00:00:24.350
sometimes but I'm mostly
successful in drawing.

00:00:24.350 --> 00:00:27.980
I think I have a pretty
strong chance at being good

00:00:27.980 --> 00:00:31.490
at this because of an
eye for design and color.

00:00:31.490 --> 00:00:32.680
- [Narrator] There are rules.

00:00:32.680 --> 00:00:34.109
- [Ray] No rules.

00:00:34.109 --> 00:00:35.291
- [Maggie] Rules.

00:00:35.291 --> 00:00:37.920
(happy, upbeat music)

00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:38.753
- [Ray] Ooooh.

00:00:38.753 --> 00:00:39.586
- [Maggie] What? Four?

00:00:39.586 --> 00:00:41.029
((happy, upbeat music)

00:00:41.029 --> 00:00:42.091
(ding)

00:00:42.091 --> 00:00:45.503
- [Ray] Oooh, prom.
- [Maggie] Prom!

00:00:45.503 --> 00:00:50.490
Prom is like celebrating high
school and how great it was.

00:00:50.490 --> 00:00:51.323
- [Narrator] Go!

00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:54.280
- [Ray] I remember going
to a Midnight Rendezvous

00:00:54.280 --> 00:00:56.432
themed prom and I wanted to
incorporate that into my mini

00:00:56.432 --> 00:00:57.510
cake.

00:00:57.510 --> 00:00:58.930
- [Maggie] For my cakes,
I'm going to decorate them

00:00:58.930 --> 00:01:01.910
to look like Coke cans
because teenagers like things

00:01:01.910 --> 00:01:04.120
that look like other things.

00:01:04.120 --> 00:01:05.320
I'm definitely going to stack it up,

00:01:05.320 --> 00:01:06.950
like on top of each other,

00:01:06.950 --> 00:01:09.649
I'd kind of like it to be a cylinder.

00:01:09.649 --> 00:01:12.740
I made the first cut, I'm scared.

00:01:12.740 --> 00:01:14.480
- [Ray] Oh, you didn't measure.

00:01:14.480 --> 00:01:15.390
- [Maggie] Huh?

00:01:15.390 --> 00:01:16.411
- [Ray] Nothing.

00:01:16.411 --> 00:01:17.244
- [Maggie] I'm supposed to measure?

00:01:17.244 --> 00:01:18.720
- [Ray] I'm measuring. I'm
measuring just because we're

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:21.704
making four of the same thing.

00:01:21.704 --> 00:01:23.707
- [Maggie] (hesitant laughter)

00:01:23.707 --> 00:01:26.540
(electronic jazz)

00:01:30.750 --> 00:01:34.210
The first prom that I could have gone to,

00:01:34.210 --> 00:01:38.080
I got grounded because I
was on Facebook too much

00:01:38.080 --> 00:01:39.140
and I wasn't studying.

00:01:39.140 --> 00:01:41.410
- [Ray] I want to probably
stick to like a dirty coat,

00:01:41.410 --> 00:01:43.730
like a naked drip kind of look for this.

00:01:43.730 --> 00:01:45.379
- [Maggie] Dirty and naked.

00:01:45.379 --> 00:01:46.212
- [Ray] Pretty much.

00:01:46.212 --> 00:01:47.219
- [Maggie] (giggles)

00:01:47.219 --> 00:01:50.052
(electronic jazz)

00:02:10.070 --> 00:02:10.903
Looks pretty okay.

00:02:10.903 --> 00:02:12.370
I've got my tower of cakes.

00:02:12.370 --> 00:02:14.350
I'm going to roll some fondant,

00:02:14.350 --> 00:02:17.260
because fondant doesn't taste
great but it looks good.

00:02:17.260 --> 00:02:19.050
Wait, do I need to do a crumb coat?

00:02:19.050 --> 00:02:19.990
What's a crumb coat?

00:02:19.990 --> 00:02:20.823
- [Ray] Yes.

00:02:20.823 --> 00:02:22.000
- [Maggie] (laughs) Thanks Ray!

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:24.290
- [Ray] Feeling like this
is messier than I thought,

00:02:24.290 --> 00:02:27.440
originally, just because
I'm not used to working

00:02:27.440 --> 00:02:28.910
with things so tiny.

00:02:28.910 --> 00:02:30.450
Overall, I think I'm on track.

00:02:30.450 --> 00:02:32.450
- [Maggie] I think it's going pretty okay.

00:02:32.450 --> 00:02:34.030
I like how the shape's turning out.

00:02:34.030 --> 00:02:37.530
It's not as even as I
want it to be but I think

00:02:37.530 --> 00:02:39.620
this is going in the right direction.

00:02:39.620 --> 00:02:42.610
- [Ray] I really am not
great with fondant so I feel

00:02:42.610 --> 00:02:44.850
like I am going to just
play off of my strengths

00:02:44.850 --> 00:02:46.773
and work with icing and buttercream.

00:02:48.490 --> 00:02:51.990
I'm going to try to place
this on top of my cake now.

00:02:51.990 --> 00:02:54.463
Going to try to do this,

00:02:58.360 --> 00:03:00.327
Aha!

00:03:00.327 --> 00:03:02.330
That's even-ish.

00:03:02.330 --> 00:03:05.150
- [Maggie] Things are
falling apart a little bit.

00:03:05.150 --> 00:03:07.720
Nothing I can't handle but like,

00:03:07.720 --> 00:03:11.172
I'm just trying to figure it out as I go.

00:03:11.172 --> 00:03:14.089
(funky jazz music)

00:03:23.120 --> 00:03:25.270
- [Ray] That's really
good fondant work though.

00:03:25.270 --> 00:03:26.510
- [Maggie] Thank you.

00:03:26.510 --> 00:03:27.640
- [Ray] Better than I can do.

00:03:27.640 --> 00:03:29.390
We're being very British
right now by being nice to

00:03:29.390 --> 00:03:31.140
each other during this competition.

00:03:33.285 --> 00:03:34.118
What?
- [Maggie] What?

00:03:34.118 --> 00:03:35.143
- [Ray] Why?

00:03:37.465 --> 00:03:40.684
Nooooooo, what?

00:03:40.684 --> 00:03:43.830
- [Maggie] Oooh. Okay.
- [Ray] Okay.

00:03:43.830 --> 00:03:46.220
Yeah, you know what, I can do this.

00:03:46.220 --> 00:03:49.361
I made these little
crescent fondant things

00:03:49.361 --> 00:03:52.500
and maybe I'm just going
to have it so it rests

00:03:52.500 --> 00:03:56.392
on the gummy on top of the cake.

00:03:56.392 --> 00:03:58.130
- [Maggie] I'm sweating,

00:03:58.130 --> 00:03:59.302
So hard right now.

00:03:59.302 --> 00:04:01.969
(electric jazz)

00:04:06.913 --> 00:04:10.163
(funky electric music)

00:04:30.950 --> 00:04:31.783
We're done.

00:04:31.783 --> 00:04:33.090
- [Ray] We did it.

00:04:33.090 --> 00:04:35.110
- [Maggie] We did it, okay.

00:04:35.110 --> 00:04:37.050
- [Ray] I think I did pretty okay.

00:04:37.050 --> 00:04:39.650
I just took what I knew and made it into

00:04:39.650 --> 00:04:40.760
a smaller cake.

00:04:40.760 --> 00:04:43.210
I feel like they're
miniature versions of cakes

00:04:43.210 --> 00:04:44.670
that I usually would make.

00:04:44.670 --> 00:04:47.350
I think I did a pretty
good job trying to make

00:04:47.350 --> 00:04:49.530
four identical cakes.

00:04:49.530 --> 00:04:51.030
I went a little overboard
with the buttercream,

00:04:51.030 --> 00:04:54.610
in the end but overall
I'm pretty happy with it.

00:04:54.610 --> 00:04:56.170
- [Maggie] It was a learning process.

00:04:56.170 --> 00:04:57.951
I think I did okay.

00:04:57.951 --> 00:05:00.570
I did better than I feared.

00:05:00.570 --> 00:05:02.440
I think I set myself for a lot,

00:05:02.440 --> 00:05:04.400
bit off more than I can chew

00:05:04.400 --> 00:05:06.620
and I think I did chew.

00:05:06.620 --> 00:05:08.712
- [Ray] We'll see how the judging goes.

00:05:08.712 --> 00:05:09.841
(ding)

00:05:09.841 --> 00:05:10.674
(happy music)

00:05:10.674 --> 00:05:12.110
- [Judge 1] This one, the Coke,

00:05:12.110 --> 00:05:15.580
I'm into a little more like modern.

00:05:15.580 --> 00:05:17.370
And you could always
sneak alcohol into prom

00:05:17.370 --> 00:05:18.420
in a Coke can.

00:05:18.420 --> 00:05:21.150
So yeah, I'm feeling like
this one is a little more me.

00:05:21.150 --> 00:05:22.530
- [Judge 2] I would say that
the Coke can is definitely

00:05:22.530 --> 00:05:23.590
more of an original idea,

00:05:23.590 --> 00:05:26.950
and they used the little
gummies as a soda pop opener.

00:05:26.950 --> 00:05:29.840
So, I'm going to have to
go originality here, but

00:05:29.840 --> 00:05:31.560
I'd be more excited about this cake.

00:05:31.560 --> 00:05:33.300
- [Judge 3] I like the
lettering of this one a lot.

00:05:33.300 --> 00:05:36.130
The color's good, very iconic, beauty,

00:05:36.130 --> 00:05:37.760
good tab detail.

00:05:37.760 --> 00:05:40.770
These ones look like little wedding cakes,

00:05:40.770 --> 00:05:42.660
which I guess is kind of prom-my.

00:05:42.660 --> 00:05:45.160
This is like Instagram-y and also,

00:05:45.160 --> 00:05:46.260
I hate that I just said that.

00:05:46.260 --> 00:05:47.570
Please, don't put that in the video.

00:05:47.570 --> 00:05:51.300
This one is much more thematically cool.

00:05:51.300 --> 00:05:52.520
- [Judge 4] I don't know
who was drinking Coke

00:05:52.520 --> 00:05:54.110
at prom, but...

00:05:54.110 --> 00:05:58.840
Maybe their prom theme
was like "Twilight Moon"?

00:05:58.840 --> 00:06:00.883
For prom, I guess I'm picking this one.

00:06:01.874 --> 00:06:03.290
- [Judge 5] I like it when
people make cakes that

00:06:03.290 --> 00:06:05.250
look like something you shouldn't eat.

00:06:05.250 --> 00:06:07.503
Both, very good, I think I'm
going to give it to these.

00:06:07.503 --> 00:06:10.980
These are really knock my socks off.

00:06:10.980 --> 00:06:12.300
- [Ray] I feel like we
should be holding hands

00:06:12.300 --> 00:06:13.842
like we're at a pageant.

00:06:13.842 --> 00:06:15.700
- [Maggie] (giggles) No
matter what happens...

00:06:15.700 --> 00:06:17.033
- [Ray] We'll still be friends!

00:06:17.033 --> 00:06:17.983
(drum roll)

00:06:17.983 --> 00:06:19.520
(kazoo)

00:06:19.520 --> 00:06:22.063
Awww, it's a cake.

00:06:22.063 --> 00:06:23.031
Oh.

00:06:23.031 --> 00:06:24.531
- [Maggie] Ohhhhh.

00:06:25.960 --> 00:06:26.830
- [Ray] Bragging rights.

00:06:26.830 --> 00:06:29.083
- [Maggie] Yes. Congratulations.

00:06:31.870 --> 00:06:32.990
I had a lot of fun.

00:06:32.990 --> 00:06:36.080
This was like a really
fun learning experience.

00:06:36.080 --> 00:06:37.905
Good job.

00:06:37.905 --> 00:06:40.405
(Happy music)

00:06:51.784 --> 00:06:53.038
(Swish)

00:06:53.038 --> 00:06:53.871
(Squeak)

